te]} {:db/id "q-162397" :question/id #uuid "ed79e8c4-1810-5f03-9522-5e9ee679d4fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-162397" :question/problem "Find the radius of the curvature for the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\,1-t⟩$ at $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{3},\\,y(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =3{t}^{2},\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =6t,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|3{t}^{2}\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 6t|}{{((3t)^{2}+(1)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6|t|}{{(9{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =\\frac{6|1|}{{(9(1)^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{(10)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{1}{κ(1)}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{10}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162397/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36986a18-172c-5983-8f6f-3211b6e8f89d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162397"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162404/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "773def70-5a39-5307-9598-15eab7739e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162404/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "508ecb4c-d393-56c5-a1af-61933c093906" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162404/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" :answer/id #uuid "bf2ce6c9-53bf-5201-91e4-f367f6b28307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162404/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "aae1ac6c-09e7-52fc-99b9-ee15048fd8ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162404/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "5e31722f-307c-5cf7-92ad-6f573d132cf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162404/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93907cfe-e575-578b-afea-70371bb607a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162404/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer-field/choices ["q-162404/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-162404/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-162404/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" "q-162404/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-162404/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162404" :question/id #uuid "29db884d-f24f-5424-973a-7e7c3098abfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-162404" :question/problem "Find the radius of curvature for the curve $r(t)=({t}^{2}-1)\\,i+(1-t)\\,j$ at $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-1,\\,y(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2t,\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2t\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 2|}{{((2t)^{2}+(-1)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(4{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{2}{{(4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(1+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{κ(\\frac{1}{2})}=\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162404/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36986a18-172c-5983-8f6f-3211b6e8f89d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162404"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162405/selection/7a548eb628a6ae5b36df4afacebe02dfd9d3a3ffeb47b85e04cfc6643b0d0895" :answer/id #uuid "ed71f44e-3adb-5719-a944-b27d60c25a6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162405/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "0c8e0038-3ef5-5231-8611-ed7c6a67146d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162405/selection/22d71a326eae3e4c21d5dec8eebaeb578c1328932031ddda12f2a1503db72424" :answer/id #uuid "833ae50e-3658-5883-b5aa-3d37893739de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162405/selection/1bebecec1d0b0808c68826d74d4c2f7770d217cc372d75ad0a52c41622ab6cc8" :answer/id #uuid "f084a609-33b1-550f-8035-8938e3a8869f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162405/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "d8eddfa4-0f66-5842-84a3-70b6639e2bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162405/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2696a603-3060-5aba-87e7-751979e9a935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162405/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-162405/selection/7a548eb628a6ae5b36df4afacebe02dfd9d3a3ffeb47b85e04cfc6643b0d0895" "q-162405/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-162405/selection/22d71a326eae3e4c21d5dec8eebaeb578c1328932031ddda12f2a1503db72424" "q-162405/selection/1bebecec1d0b0808c68826d74d4c2f7770d217cc372d75ad0a52c41622ab6cc8" "q-162405/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162405" :question/id #uuid "59fdd5af-44ff-5ffd-94d6-223f05abf6d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-162405" :question/problem "Find the radius of curvature for the curve $r(t)=(1+t)^{2}\\,i+(1-t)^{2}\\,j$ at $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=(1+t)^{2},\\,y(t)=(1-t)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2(1+t),\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-2(1-t) \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2(1+t)\\cdot 2-(-2(1-t))\\cdot 2|}{{(\\,(2(1+t))^{2}+(2(1-t))^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{(8+8{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{8}{{(8+8(0)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{(8+0)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{1}{κ(0)}=2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162405/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36986a18-172c-5983-8f6f-3211b6e8f89d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162532/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "3ad617fe-efc9-5076-8c27-09cc8636d85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162532/selection/4bd87ad5cdff0b2d0aa7574d5c7450ac33fa34774f895ce16d251ca09a1932ec" :answer/id #uuid "c254025a-acff-5311-a369-5cf0e944fc97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162532/selection/22879df45f12d03caa6fc4777f904520a0b72bbf0f4efea7d9e05060b02279fe" :answer/id #uuid "c02e1f2a-12ee-5e0f-adc8-3dcc113e63ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162532/selection/9ff3c1bd757d17ad7f8af335cb950f7af824aa6d01208010f2d0b75976b02c4f" :answer/id #uuid "ec57e9dd-ba68-54ed-be3b-e96492c65ad8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162532/selection/2ba67ff54273661460eaa0e3e45c1c4442f0b6f49f7edadb98be753769c4c9a1" :answer/id #uuid "ef3b0f1d-02ab-5f7f-b939-56146e3d4818" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162532/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f3961c7-a34f-5cd8-b14a-5d66c9a394e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162532/selection/22879df45f12d03caa6fc4777f904520a0b72bbf0f4efea7d9e05060b02279fe" :answer-field/choices ["q-162532/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-162532/selection/4bd87ad5cdff0b2d0aa7574d5c7450ac33fa34774f895ce16d251ca09a1932ec" "q-162532/selection/22879df45f12d03caa6fc4777f904520a0b72bbf0f4efea7d9e05060b02279fe" "q-162532/selection/9ff3c1bd757d17ad7f8af335cb950f7af824aa6d01208010f2d0b75976b02c4f" "q-162532/selection/2ba67ff54273661460eaa0e3e45c1c4442f0b6f49f7edadb98be753769c4c9a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162532" :question/id #uuid "158b5a12-e0e4-56c7-80c7-4700e06df09f" :question/math-academy-id "q-162532" :question/problem "Find the signed curvature of the curve $y=x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ at $x=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "The signed curvature $k(x)$ of a plane curve $y=y(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nk(x)=\\frac{{y}^{″}(x)}{(1+[{y}^{′}(x)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${y}^{′}(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x):$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,{y}^{″}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the signed curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(x) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{[1+{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{2}]}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(0) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{{[1+{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))}^{2}]}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{{2}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-162532/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384072a8-f008-5279-bb58-8086eb42b710"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162532"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162535/selection/43cdd7b9f2fd0d514c4d3783c209451bb6e62883a7f2d1812a4a864e5f592ad2" :answer/id #uuid "5e7924ef-f982-5292-8cbc-dee50f7629eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{e}{({e}^{2}-e+2)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162535/selection/9883f034b7d2c8a05505229a43cbfe47186721fc4de12159bf0e6a17af84b7ef" :answer/id #uuid "517b8ae7-f429-5017-af57-43ba0b92d5e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{({e}^{2}-2e+2)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162535/selection/013f0c0c3bfa274074d955c9a863f638edb96100c3b6c75a6689deb050a07a5c" :answer/id #uuid "3ae907fd-e176-5a15-9783-082a6686e768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{e}{({e}^{2}-e+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162535/selection/5a4320d05210f279427bad9744e57ad5387d77625826e1953521d92ec55846f5" :answer/id #uuid "0b95d3db-c026-5d02-903f-53dbdeb7c332" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{({e}^{2}-e+2)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162535/selection/1cb89f181a00547016fe306d8048635c5a4fe76ed86cfdd4b8d3e8f0e989851c" :answer/id #uuid "ac6ee906-ce06-59af-9494-631588201eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{e}{({e}^{2}-2e+2)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162535/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9479c27e-6a60-5b76-9bb7-d18536fff57c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162535/selection/1cb89f181a00547016fe306d8048635c5a4fe76ed86cfdd4b8d3e8f0e989851c" :answer-field/choices ["q-162535/selection/43cdd7b9f2fd0d514c4d3783c209451bb6e62883a7f2d1812a4a864e5f592ad2" "q-162535/selection/9883f034b7d2c8a05505229a43cbfe47186721fc4de12159bf0e6a17af84b7ef" "q-162535/selection/013f0c0c3bfa274074d955c9a863f638edb96100c3b6c75a6689deb050a07a5c" "q-162535/selection/5a4320d05210f279427bad9744e57ad5387d77625826e1953521d92ec55846f5" "q-162535/selection/1cb89f181a00547016fe306d8048635c5a4fe76ed86cfdd4b8d3e8f0e989851c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162535" :question/id #uuid "9efc8285-3803-5a6e-9693-e78f932370e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162535" :question/problem "Find the signed curvature of the curve $y=x-{e}^{x}$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The signed curvature $k(x)$ of a plane curve $y=y(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nk(x)=\\frac{{y}^{″}(x)}{(1+[{y}^{′}(x)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${y}^{′}(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x):$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=1-{e}^{x},\\,{y}^{″}(x)=-{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the signed curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(x) & =\\frac{-{e}^{x}}{{[1+{(1-{e}^{x})}^{2}]}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{(1+1+{e}^{2x}-2{e}^{x})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{(2+{e}^{2x}-2{e}^{x})}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(1) & =-\\frac{{e}^{(1)}}{{(2+{e}^{2(1)}-2{e}^{(1)})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{e}{({e}^{2}-2e+2)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-162535/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "384072a8-f008-5279-bb58-8086eb42b710"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162535"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
